    "created_at": "2026-03-10T15:46:03Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-03-10T15:46:03Z",
    "body": "I'd like to discuss https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/12437, particularly to decide on one of the two approaches (see this [summary comment](https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/12437#issuecomment-3725014807) and the [notes from the ARIA deep dive](https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/12437#issuecomment-4009607664)):\n\n\n1. **`::interest-button` pseudo element.** \n    - E.g.: `<a href=\"\" interestfor=id></a> <style>a::interest-button {content: \"?\"}</style>`\n    - **Pros**: Can have the correct focus/a11y behavior by default, and hard to mess up (no HTML/JS access). Can be \"on by default\". Can have accessible styles (e.g. tap target sizes) by default.\n    - **Cons**: Positioning is constrained - always shows up in a particular relative position (after the element, before ::after). Feels weird to add a pseudo element on all elements (but only originated on `<a interestfor>` and `<button interestfor>`). \n2. **`<span interestbutton>` attribute.**\n    - E.g.: `<a href=\"\" interestfor=id>Link text <span interestbutton> ? </span></a>`\n    - **Pros**: Can have the correct focus/a11y behavior by default. Can have accessible styles (e.g. tap target sizes) by default. Can be placed anywhere within the invoker element. \n    - **Cons**: I assume it does nothing when the span isn't within an interest invoker? Doesn't work for `<input type=button>` (maybe [ok](https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/11053)). Cannot be \"on by default\".\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
